From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Data - GProp_SelGProps and GProp_VelGProps compute
 the matrix of inertia, and for the volume the centre of mass, of a gp_Cone
 wrongly

GProp_SelGProps::Perform(const gp_Cone&, ...) and GProp_VelGProps::Perform(const
gp_Cone&, ...) build Dm, the matrix of inertia about the location of the cone in
the axes of the cone, from closed forms that do not integrate to anything, and
then assemble inertia from it in a way that is wrong for any Dm. On gp_Cone,
P(u, v) = Loc + (R + v sin a)(cos u X + sin u Y) + v cos a Z, so with
r = R + v sin a and z = v cos a the surface element is r dv du, and the volume
swept between the axis and the patch (the convention the cylinder and sphere
overloads of GProp_VelGProps use, and 0051 documents) is dV = rho drho du dz.

Per unit angle the surface moments are

  Dm(3,3) = int r^3 dv           = (Z2 - Z1)(R1^3 + R1^2 R2 + R1 R2^2 + R2^3) / 4
  int z^2 dA = cos^2 a (Z2 - Z1)(R Auxi2 + sin a (Z2^3 + Z2^2 Z1 + Z2 Z1^2 + Z1^3) / 4)
  int x z dA = cos a (Z2 - Z1)(R^2 (Z1 + Z2) / 2 + 2 R sin a Auxi2
               + sin^2 a (Z1 + Z2)(Z1^2 + Z2^2) / 4) (Sn2 - Sn1)

and the volume moments are

  Dm(3,3) = cos a (Z2 - Z1)(R1^4 + R1^3 R2 + R1^2 R2^2 + R1 R2^3 + R2^4) / 20
  int z^2 dV = cos^3 a / 2 int v^2 r^2 dv
  int x z dV = cos^2 a / 3 int v r^3 dv (Sn2 - Sn1)

with R1 = R + Z1 sin a, R2 = R + Z2 sin a and Auxi2 = (Z2^2 + Z1 Z2 + Z1^2) / 3.
Against those the code has these defects, all in the two cone overloads:

  - GProp_SelGProps: IR2 carries an extra cos a sin a, so Dm(3,3) is that
    fraction of the second moment about the axis. IZ2 carries an extra
    (Z2 - Z1) cos a and divides both terms by 4, where only the sin a term takes
    it. ISn2 repeats ICn2, with a plus where the sine integral has a minus.
    ICnSn is (Cn2^2 - Cn1^2) where the integral is (Sn2^2 - Sn1^2) / 2.
    ICnz and ISnz are a different polynomial. The x and y coordinate of the
    centre of mass uses sin a Auxi2 where the quadratic term is sin^2 a Auxi2,
    which a full turn hides because it multiplies sin u and cos u terms that
    integrate to zero.
  - GProp_VelGProps: the centre of mass is the one of the lateral surface, not of
    the solid, in all three coordinates. IR2 is a four term cubic over 4 with a
    spurious sin a where the moment is a five term quartic over 20, and ISn2,
    IZ2, ICnSn, ICnz and ISnz are wrong as above.
  - Both: inertia is built as gp_Mat(rows of lambda_i * v_i) from the Jacobi
    decomposition of Dm, which is diag(lambda) V^T and not V diag(lambda) V^T, so
    the sign Jacobi happens to give an eigenvector changes the matrix, and Dm,
    which is about the location of the cone, is added to the Huyghens term of the
    centre of mass as if it were already about the centre of mass.

The patch computes every entry from the integrals above and assembles
inertia = P Dm P^T - H(g, Location) + H(g, loc), with P the columns of the axes of
the cone and H the GProp::HOperator term, which is the matrix of inertia about
loc whatever loc is. The mass is not touched (0050 and 0051). The cylinder,
sphere and torus overloads are not touched either; see the end.

GProp_VelGProps and GProp_SelGProps have no caller anywhere in the OCCT tree, so
there is no call site whose use of the result could settle the convention. The
arbiter is an independent Gauss-Legendre integral over the parameter space of
the cone, which shares no formula with the code above.

Measured on macOS arm64 against V8_0_1 with 0050 and 0051 applied and the
translation units override-linked, gp_Cone(gp::XOY(), pi/6, 5) over u in
[0, 2 pi], v in [0, 10]. Dm(3,3) of the surface: before 12753.276779771842,
after 29452.431127404328, the integral 29452.431127404328 (the ratio before is
0.43301270189221902, cos(pi/6) sin(pi/6)). Largest entry of the matrix of
inertia about the centre of mass, relative to the integral: before 2.5
(GProp_SelGProps) and 2.4 (GProp_VelGProps), after 1.2e-15 and 6.3e-15. The z
coordinate of the centre of mass of the solid: before 4.81125224325, after
5.25801138012, the integral 5.25801138012. Over 64 checks (semi-angles pi/3,
pi/6, pi/12, -pi/6, -pi/12 and -pi/4, full and partial turns, the frame of the
cone untilted and tilted, loc at the origin and at (2, -1, 3), mass, centre of
mass, matrix of inertia and a moment about an oblique axis) 64 fail before and 0
fail after, the largest deviation 7.9e-14.

The same probe on gp_Cylinder and gp_Sphere (16 checks) fails 16 of 16 too: for
the full gp_Cylinder surface of radius 5 and height 10 Dm(3,3) reads 314.159,
which is 2 pi R H, where the second moment about the axis is 2 pi R^3 H, and the
signs of the matrix come out of the same eigenvector assembly. That is measured
and not diagnosed or fixed here: the cone is one defect cluster and the other
overloads are another.

The reproducer is Scripts/repro/3010-cone-inertia/probe.cxx and the transcript is
Scripts/repro/3010-cone-inertia/transcript.txt in the OCCTSwift repository.
OCCTSwift issue #3010. It applies on top of 0050 and 0051 and not without them,
since its hunks take their context from the lines those two change.

diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_SelGProps.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_SelGProps.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_SelGProps.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_SelGProps.cxx
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@ void GProp_SelGProps::Perform(const gp_Cone& S,
   // |dP/du ^ dP/dv| is R + v sin(a) on gp_Cone, so the area carries no cos(a) factor.
   dim = (Alpha2 - Alpha1) * (Z2 - Z1) * Auxi1;

-  double Ix = (R * R + R * (Z2 + Z1) * Snt + Snt * Auxi2) / Auxi1;
+  double Ix = (R * R + R * (Z2 + Z1) * Snt + Snt * Snt * Auxi2) / Auxi1;
   double Iy = Ix * (Cn1 - Cn2) / (Alpha2 - Alpha1);
   Ix        = Ix * (Sn2 - Sn1) / (Alpha2 - Alpha1);
   double Iz = Cnt * (R * (Z2 + Z1) / 2. + Snt * Auxi2) / Auxi1;
@@ -134,18 +134,21 @@ void GProp_SelGProps::Perform(const gp_Cone& S,
              Y0 + Ya1 * Ix + Ya2 * Iy + Ya3 * Iz,
              Z0 + Za1 * Ix + Za2 * Iy + Za3 * Iz);

-  double R1   = R + Z1 * Snt;
-  double R2   = R + Z2 * Snt;
-  double ZZ   = (Z2 - Z1) * Cnt;
-  double IR2  = ZZ * Snt * (R1 * R1 * R1 + R1 * R1 * R2 + R1 * R2 * R2 + R2 * R2 * R2) / 4.;
-  double ICn2 = IR2 * (Alpha2 - Alpha1 + Cn2 * Sn2 - Cn1 * Sn1) / 2.;
-  double ISn2 = IR2 * (Alpha2 - Alpha1 + Cn2 * Sn2 - Cn1 * Sn1) / 2.;
-  double IZ2  = ZZ * Cnt * Cnt * (Z2 - Z1) * (Alpha2 - Alpha1)
-               * (R * Auxi2 + Snt * (Z2 * Z2 * Z2 + Z2 * Z2 * Z1 + Z2 * Z1 * Z1 + Z1 * Z1 * Z1))
-               / 4.;
-  double ICnSn = IR2 * (Cn2 * Cn2 - Cn1 * Cn1);
-  double ICnz  = Cnt * Snt * ZZ * (R * (Z1 + Z2) / 2. + Auxi2) * (Sn2 - Sn1);
-  double ISnz  = Cnt * Snt * ZZ * (R * (Z1 + Z2) / 2. + Auxi2) * (Cn1 - Cn2);
+  double R1 = R + Z1 * Snt;
+  double R2 = R + Z2 * Snt;
+  double Z3 = Z2 * Z2 * Z2 + Z2 * Z2 * Z1 + Z2 * Z1 * Z1 + Z1 * Z1 * Z1;
+  double Z4 = (Z1 + Z2) * (Z1 * Z1 + Z2 * Z2);
+  // Per unit angle, over the generatrix with r = R + v sin(a), z = v cos(a), dA = r dv du:
+  // IR2 = int r^3 dv, IZ2 = int z^2 r dv, IRZ = int r z r dv.
+  double IR2 = (Z2 - Z1) * (R1 * R1 * R1 + R1 * R1 * R2 + R1 * R2 * R2 + R2 * R2 * R2) / 4.;
+  double IRZ =
+    Cnt * (Z2 - Z1) * (R * R * (Z1 + Z2) / 2. + 2. * R * Snt * Auxi2 + Snt * Snt * Z4 / 4.);
+  double ICn2  = IR2 * (Alpha2 - Alpha1 + Cn2 * Sn2 - Cn1 * Sn1) / 2.;
+  double ISn2  = IR2 * (Alpha2 - Alpha1 - Cn2 * Sn2 + Cn1 * Sn1) / 2.;
+  double IZ2   = Cnt * Cnt * (Z2 - Z1) * (Alpha2 - Alpha1) * (R * Auxi2 + Snt * Z3 / 4.);
+  double ICnSn = IR2 * (Sn2 * Sn2 - Sn1 * Sn1) / 2.;
+  double ICnz  = IRZ * (Sn2 - Sn1);
+  double ISnz  = IRZ * (Cn1 - Cn2);

   math_Matrix Dm(1, 3, 1, 3);
   Dm(1, 1) = ISn2 + IZ2;
@@ -155,32 +158,14 @@ void GProp_SelGProps::Perform(const gp_Cone& S,
   Dm(1, 3) = Dm(3, 1) = -ICnz;
   Dm(3, 2) = Dm(2, 3) = -ISnz;

-  math_Matrix Passage(1, 3, 1, 3);
-  Passage(1, 1) = Xa1;
-  Passage(1, 2) = Xa2;
-  Passage(1, 3) = Xa3;
-  Passage(2, 1) = Ya1;
-  Passage(2, 2) = Ya2;
-  Passage(2, 3) = Ya3;
-  Passage(3, 1) = Za1;
-  Passage(3, 2) = Za2;
-  Passage(3, 3) = Za3;
-
-  math_Jacobi J(Dm);
-  math_Vector V1(1, 3), V2(1, 3), V3(1, 3);
-  J.Vector(1, V1);
-  V1.Multiply(Passage, V1);
-  V1.Multiply(J.Value(1));
-  J.Vector(2, V2);
-  V2.Multiply(Passage, V2);
-  V2.Multiply(J.Value(2));
-  J.Vector(3, V3);
-  V3.Multiply(Passage, V3);
-  V3.Multiply(J.Value(3));
-
-  inertia =
-    gp_Mat(gp_XYZ(V1(1), V2(1), V3(1)), gp_XYZ(V1(2), V2(2), V3(2)), gp_XYZ(V1(3), V2(3), V3(3)));
+  // Dm is the matrix of inertia about the location of the cone, in the axes of the cone. Take it to
+  // the global axes, then to the centre of mass and from there to loc.
+  gp_Mat Pm(Xa1, Xa2, Xa3, Ya1, Ya2, Ya3, Za1, Za2, Za3);
+  gp_Mat
+    Dg(Dm(1, 1), Dm(1, 2), Dm(1, 3), Dm(2, 1), Dm(2, 2), Dm(2, 3), Dm(3, 1), Dm(3, 2), Dm(3, 3));
   gp_Mat Hop;
+  GProp::HOperator(g, S.Location(), dim, Hop);
+  inertia = Pm * Dg * Pm.Transposed() - Hop;
   GProp::HOperator(g, loc, dim, Hop);
   inertia = inertia + Hop;
 }
diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_VelGProps.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_VelGProps.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_VelGProps.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_VelGProps.cxx
@@ -165,8 +165,7 @@ void GProp_VelGProps::Perform(const gp_Cone& S,
   double Sn1   = std::sin(Alpha1);
   double Cn2   = std::cos(Alpha2);
   double Cn1   = std::cos(Alpha1);
-  double ZZ    = (Z2 - Z1) * (Z2 - Z1) * Cnt * Snt;
-  double Auxi1 = 2 * R + (Z2 + Z1) * Snt;
+  double Auxi2 = (Z2 * Z2 + Z1 * Z2 + Z1 * Z1) / 3.;

   // Frustum volume pi/3 H (R1^2 + R1 R2 + R2^2); the old form carried sin(a) and vanished at a = 0.
   dim = (Alpha2 - Alpha1) * Cnt * (Z2 - Z1)
@@ -174,24 +173,38 @@ void GProp_VelGProps::Perform(const gp_Cone& S,

   double R1    = R + Z1 * Snt;
   double R2    = R + Z2 * Snt;
+  double Z4    = (Z1 + Z2) * (Z1 * Z1 + Z2 * Z2);
+  double Z5    = Z2 * Z2 * Z2 * Z2 + Z2 * Z2 * Z2 * Z1 + Z2 * Z2 * Z1 * Z1 + Z2 * Z1 * Z1 * Z1
+                 + Z1 * Z1 * Z1 * Z1;
   double Coef0 = (R1 * R1 + R1 * R2 + R2 * R2);
-  double Iz    = Cnt * (R * (Z2 + Z1) + 2 * Snt * (Z1 * Z1 + Z1 * Z2 + Z2 * Z2) / 3.) / Auxi1;
-  double Ix    = Coef0 * (Sn2 - Sn1) / (Alpha2 - Alpha1) / Auxi1;
-  double Iy    = Coef0 * (Cn1 - Cn2) / (Alpha2 - Alpha1) / Auxi1;
+  double Coef1 = (R1 * R1 * R1 + R1 * R1 * R2 + R1 * R2 * R2 + R2 * R2 * R2);
+  // int v r^2 dv over (Z2 - Z1), r = R + v sin(a): the z moment of the frustum.
+  double Coef2 = R * R * (Z1 + Z2) / 2. + 2. * R * Snt * Auxi2 + Snt * Snt * Z4 / 4.;
+  double Iz    = 3. * Cnt * Coef2 / Coef0;
+  double Ix    = Coef1 * (Sn2 - Sn1) / (Alpha2 - Alpha1) / (2. * Coef0);
+  double Iy    = Coef1 * (Cn1 - Cn2) / (Alpha2 - Alpha1) / (2. * Coef0);

   g.SetCoord(X0 + Xa1 * Ix + Xa2 * Iy + Xa3 * Iz,
              Y0 + Ya1 * Ix + Ya2 * Iy + Ya3 * Iz,
              Z0 + Za1 * Ix + Za2 * Iy + Za3 * Iz);

-  double IR2  = ZZ * (R2 * R2 * R2 + R2 * R2 * R1 + R1 * R1 * R2 + R1 * R1 * R1) / 4.;
-  double ICn2 = IR2 * (Alpha2 - Alpha1 + Cn2 * Sn2 - Cn1 * Sn1) / 2.;
-  double ISn2 = IR2 * (Alpha2 - Alpha1 + Cn2 * Sn2 - Cn1 * Sn1) / 2.;
-  double IZ2  = ZZ * Cnt * Cnt * (Alpha2 - Alpha1)
-               * (Z1 * Z1 * (R / 3 + Z1 * Snt / 4) + Z2 * Z2 * (R / 3 + Z2 * Snt / 4)
-                  + Z1 * Z2 * (R / 3 + Z1 * Snt / 4 + Z2 * Snt / 4));
-  double ICnSn = IR2 * (Cn2 * Cn2 - Cn1 * Cn1);
-  double ICnz  = (Z1 + Z2) * ZZ * Coef0 * (Sn2 - Sn1) / 3;
-  double ISnz  = (Z1 + Z2) * ZZ * Coef0 * (Cn1 - Cn2) / 3;
+  // Per unit angle, over the frustum with r = R + v sin(a), z = v cos(a), dV = rho drho du dz:
+  // IR2 = int r^4/4 dz, IZ2 = int z^2 r^2/2 dz, IRZ = int z r^3/3 dz.
+  double IR2   = Cnt * (Z2 - Z1)
+                 * (R2 * R2 * R2 * R2 + R2 * R2 * R2 * R1 + R2 * R2 * R1 * R1 + R2 * R1 * R1 * R1
+                    + R1 * R1 * R1 * R1)
+                 / 20.;
+  double IRZ   = Cnt * Cnt * (Z2 - Z1)
+                 * (R * R * R * (Z1 + Z2) / 2. + 3. * R * R * Snt * Auxi2
+                    + 3. * R * Snt * Snt * Z4 / 4. + Snt * Snt * Snt * Z5 / 5.)
+                 / 3.;
+  double ICn2  = IR2 * (Alpha2 - Alpha1 + Cn2 * Sn2 - Cn1 * Sn1) / 2.;
+  double ISn2  = IR2 * (Alpha2 - Alpha1 - Cn2 * Sn2 + Cn1 * Sn1) / 2.;
+  double IZ2   = Cnt * Cnt * Cnt * (Z2 - Z1) * (Alpha2 - Alpha1)
+                 * (R * R * Auxi2 + R * Snt * Z4 / 2. + Snt * Snt * Z5 / 5.) / 2.;
+  double ICnSn = IR2 * (Sn2 * Sn2 - Sn1 * Sn1) / 2.;
+  double ICnz  = IRZ * (Sn2 - Sn1);
+  double ISnz  = IRZ * (Cn1 - Cn2);

   math_Matrix Dm(1, 3, 1, 3);
   Dm(1, 1) = ISn2 + IZ2;
@@ -201,32 +214,14 @@ void GProp_VelGProps::Perform(const gp_Cone& S,
   Dm(1, 3) = Dm(3, 1) = -ICnz;
   Dm(3, 2) = Dm(2, 3) = -ISnz;

-  math_Matrix Passage(1, 3, 1, 3);
-  Passage(1, 1) = Xa1;
-  Passage(1, 2) = Xa2;
-  Passage(1, 3) = Xa3;
-  Passage(2, 1) = Ya1;
-  Passage(2, 2) = Ya2;
-  Passage(2, 3) = Ya3;
-  Passage(3, 1) = Za1;
-  Passage(3, 2) = Za2;
-  Passage(3, 3) = Za3;
-
-  math_Jacobi J(Dm);
-  math_Vector V1(1, 3), V2(1, 3), V3(1, 3);
-  J.Vector(1, V1);
-  V1.Multiply(Passage, V1);
-  V1.Multiply(J.Value(1));
-  J.Vector(2, V2);
-  V2.Multiply(Passage, V2);
-  V2.Multiply(J.Value(2));
-  J.Vector(3, V3);
-  V3.Multiply(Passage, V3);
-  V3.Multiply(J.Value(3));
-
-  inertia =
-    gp_Mat(gp_XYZ(V1(1), V2(1), V3(1)), gp_XYZ(V1(2), V2(2), V3(2)), gp_XYZ(V1(3), V2(3), V3(3)));
+  // Dm is the matrix of inertia about the location of the cone, in the axes of the cone. Take it to
+  // the global axes, then to the centre of mass and from there to loc.
+  gp_Mat Pm(Xa1, Xa2, Xa3, Ya1, Ya2, Ya3, Za1, Za2, Za3);
+  gp_Mat
+    Dg(Dm(1, 1), Dm(1, 2), Dm(1, 3), Dm(2, 1), Dm(2, 2), Dm(2, 3), Dm(3, 1), Dm(3, 2), Dm(3, 3));
   gp_Mat Hop;
+  GProp::HOperator(g, S.Location(), dim, Hop);
+  inertia = Pm * Dg * Pm.Transposed() - Hop;
   GProp::HOperator(g, loc, dim, Hop);
   inertia = inertia + Hop;
 }
